{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1467689-vice-ridden-virtuous-merits-on-supernaturals","id":1467689,"title":"Vice-ridden / Virtuous merits on Supernaturals.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-13T10:03:03-08:00","id":1467689,"title":"Vice-ridden / Virtuous merits on Supernaturals.","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> Do the <b>Vice-ridden</b> or the <b>Virtuous </b>merits work on Supernaturals? Specially those that have things that are not Virtues or Vices, i.e. Thread, Needle, Dirge, Mask, Blood, Bone, etc.<br /> <br /> If either of them works, do the creatures gain an extra Vice or Virtue, or an extra equivalent characteristic?<br /> <br /> Thanks,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T10:30:15-08:00","id":1467693,"title":"","content":"No, they do not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T10:37:11-08:00","id":1467694,"title":"","content":"As a general rule, no. Given that almost every anchor in the game behaves just a little differently and don't have the limitations as Virtue and Vice, it's relatively pointless to create merits that increase the character's willpower economy, particularly since lot of that economy is baked into the conflicts of those individual games.<br /> <br /> That said, if you don't think it'll fuck up your Willpower economy too much, it might not hurt to give it whirl. The only version where it's particular issue is Deviant, where Conviction and Loyalty don't work like that.<br /> <br /> As a cheap version, Consider the Following:<br /> <br /> <b>Dual-Anchored(2-Dot Merit)</b><br /> <br /> Your character experiences are dynamic, and resulted in them having a more multi-layered sense of self to connect to in times of crisis and doubt.<br /> <b>Effect:</b> The characters may choose to have a second one of their two anchors (Mask or Dirge in Vampire, Blood or Bone in Werewolf, Elpis or Torment in Promethean, Needle or Thread in Changeling, Root or Bloom in Geist, Balance or Burden in Mummy, and Life or Legend in Beast). The second anchor obeys the rules of it's type.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-14T04:01:44-08:00","id":1467782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1467689-vice-ridden-virtuous-merits-on-supernaturals?p=1467694#post1467694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Dual-Anchored(2-Dot Merit)</b><br /> <br /> Your character experiences are dynamic, and resulted in them having a more multi-layered sense of self to connect to in times of crisis and doubt.<br /> <b>Effect:</b> The characters may choose to have a second one of their two anchors (Mask or Dirge in Vampire, Blood or Bone in Werewolf, Elpis or Torment in Promethean, Needle or Thread in Changeling, Root or Bloom in Geist, Balance or Burden in Mummy, and Life or Legend in Beast). The second anchor obeys the rules of it's type.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I were to ever run a CoD game with this in the merit roster, I\u2019d rule that only those playing as supernaturals would be able to take it (obviously) and that they\u2019d only be able to take it twice, once for each anchor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-14T12:28:18-08:00","id":1467810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerrorCooper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1467689-vice-ridden-virtuous-merits-on-supernaturals?p=1467782#post1467782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I were to ever run a CoD game with this in the merit roster, I\u2019d rule that only those playing as supernaturals would be able to take it (obviously) and that they\u2019d only be able to take it twice, once for each anchor.</div> </div> </div> </div>The supernaturals is a point that I just took as obvious, which leads to a good lesson-Never do that.<br /> <br /> As for it being taken twice, the game books tend to explain if something <i>can</i> be taken twice rather than the other way around. That said, I'm also against it being taken any more than once for two reasons-<br /> <br /> 1) That <i>does</i> feel like fucking with the willpower economy too much.<br /> 2) Vice-Ridden and Virtuous exist to say a particular thing about your character, and any sort of equivalent is there to say a similiar particular thing.<br /> <br /> The two are inter-related issues. Anchors as the main way to restore Willpower is there to incentivize character establishing moments by getting players to chase how they react in their low moments or how they step up in their high moments. Vice-Ridden and Virtuous make a character stand out, then, by showing how one characters is prone to (self-)destructive reaction towards the stressors of getting involved with the supernatural or by being exceptionally (self-)constructive in response. If a character has both of those, then it just basically means that they.....react a lot to stressors and are able to get back into it more quickly, which is not only not particularly exciting and character defining, but also means that it's not as important-the character just has too many opportunities to establish themselves to ever really be at risk for Wilpower.<br /> <br /> For characters where Anchors demonstrate the over-arching humanity vs monstrosity conflict that exists in characters (Mask vs Dirge, Elpis vs Torment*, Bloom vs Root, Life vs Legend), a character having two of one or the other shows how much more rooted in humanity or monstrosity they are, and how that negatively impacts their lives as beings who have to court both aspects. For a werewolf, they might be too into the Hunt via Blood or too removed from it via Bone. A Changeling may be too much emotionally driven by their THreads, or they might be a little too pointed and dishonest with themselves with multiple Needles. A Mummy could be shown to have been a poor choice For the Rite by their excess of Burdens, or they might have been always ready for it with their Balances. And Of Course, Deviant's don't even play nicely with the typical anchor talk. For all of these, allowing one for each side just means that they're always going and not much else.<br /> <br /> So yeah, It's a one time merit.<br /> <br /> *Arguably you could better group Elpis and Torment into the off the axis group with Werewolf, Changeling, and Mummy, because Hope Vector vs Despair Vector doesn't quite line up with the humanity vs monstrosity argument, but on the other hand, Elpis literally is what encourages you toward towards humanity where Torment encourages you to give up and stay a monster, so close enough for government work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-21T11:55:06-08:00","id":1468514,"title":"","content":"If it weren't for the issue with the Willpower economy, I would allow the Virtous/Vice-ridden merits for splats.<br /> <br /> Personally, I have mixed feelings for the supernatural Anchors. On one hand I do get that they highlight specific themes for each gameline and provide interesting descriptions to the characters, on the other hand I still think that a virtue/vice, or a more general positive/negative quality is the best way to describe a well-rounded character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1467689-vice-ridden-virtuous-merits-on-supernaturals?p=1467810#post1467810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For characters where Anchors demonstrate the over-arching humanity vs monstrosity conflict that exists in characters (Mask vs Dirge, Elpis vs Torment*, Bloom vs Root, Life vs Legend), a character having two of one or the other shows how much more rooted in humanity or monstrosity they are, and how that negatively impacts their lives as beings who have to court both aspects. For a werewolf, they might be too into the Hunt via Blood or too removed from it via Bone. A Changeling may be too much emotionally driven by their THreads, or they might be a little too pointed and dishonest with themselves with multiple Needles. A Mummy could be shown to have been a poor choice For the Rite by their excess of Burdens, or they might have been always ready for it with their Balances. And Of Course, Deviant's don't even play nicely with the typical anchor talk. For all of these, allowing one for each side just means that they're always going and not much else.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that Anchors express the dual nature of both human and monstrous sides of a character, but I wouldn't say it demonstrates its conflict. Conflict is better described by their Integrity-like traits, either top-down ones like Humanity or left-right ones like Harmony. They describe opposing forces, with lots of gray areas in-between, and with clearly established drawbacks when leaning towards at least one of its extremes (the drawback of the other usually being really hard to keep up and requiring to make sacrifices).<br /> <br /> There's nothing of the sort in Anchors. It's actually a sign of two facets of the character coexisting more or less harmoniously *. Also, while Anchors can impact negatively on the character lives because you're probably paying a price for sticking to your ideals/indulgence/behavior etc., they don't really have much of drawbacks. Considering <i>them </i>to be a sign that you're too rooted into humanity/monstruosity with all the &quot;drawbacks&quot; that it entails is a bit of a stretch, IMHO. I mean yes, in a sense it does, but a Humanity-equivalent trait is much better suited for that.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, the role of Anchors is to give players direction to their choices. Do you accept the bribe? A Vice of Greed will suggest you to do so.<br /> In that sense all anchors do their job, some better that others perhaps. One issue I can see with having too many Anchors is that instead of having better aides for roleplaying your character you end up more confused than anything.<br /> <br /> <br /> * unless you deliberately choose opposing anchors like Generous and Avarice. Even then, it mostly describes a win-win situation where either keeping your stuff or giving it away will earn you willpower anyway. Not much of a conflict if you ask me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26440,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26440-moonwhisper","user":"moonwhisper","date":". 11-21-2021, 03:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26440-moonwhisper","name":"moonwhisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-21T15:24:23-08:00","id":1468534,"title":"","content":"What would be the effect for a supernatural character to actually be able to get one of those not to add another of their Anchors, but an actual human-like Vice or Virtue?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-21T17:26:06-08:00","id":1468539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1467689-vice-ridden-virtuous-merits-on-supernaturals?p=1468534#post1468534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would be the effect for a supernatural character to actually be able to get one of those not to add another of their Anchors, but an actual human-like Vice or Virtue?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, some of them already exist.<br /> <br /> Deviant has two Merits that give you a Virtue or a Vice solely for Willpower recovery purposes (and you have to successfully roll Resolve + Composure for that), because Conviction and Loyalty pull in much more individual and mutable directions.<br /> <br /> Werewolf has the Code of Honor Merit, which gives you a Virtue for all purposes and then some, but it's got a drawback on top of having a prerequisite of Harmony 8+ (with all that implies).<br /> <br /> Mages start out with human Virtues and Vices (and gradually shift them as they raise their Gnosis), and one of the Conditions applied by Acts of Hubris gives them an extra &quot;Selfish&quot; Vice until they hurt someone important to them in a way that risks further Wisdom loss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-21T19:46:28-08:00","id":1468551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1467689-vice-ridden-virtuous-merits-on-supernaturals?p=1468539#post1468539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, some of them already exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>They exist in a sense, some, but I was curious about the straightforward path: what would be the effect on each splat to have access to the merits Virtuous and Vice-Ridden, with the direct effect of giving it a human Virtue/Vice?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T10:09:17-08:00","id":1468846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1467689-vice-ridden-virtuous-merits-on-supernaturals?p=1468551#post1468551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They exist in a sense, some, but I was curious about the straightforward path: what would be the effect on each splat to have access to the merits Virtuous and Vice-Ridden, with the direct effect of giving it a human Virtue/Vice?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It depends a lot on how it is run. They tend to have different mechanics - Vice and Virtue have separate willpower-fulfillment mechanics, where most Anchors are each binary, with a single will and full will regain condition. You'd have to determine if you can gain willpower from that Virtue/Vice separate from your other anchors, or if fulfilling a Virtue/Vice is mutually exclusive with gaining willpower of that magnitude from another anchor (that is, if you gain via a Vice, you can't regain a single willpower from your Needle or Thread). This drastically alters the nature of each game in the long run - if you can use multiple ways to get willpower back, you'll see a mechanical shift as willpower is used more often; if you get limited, you may see a thematic shift, as the Virtue/Vice may become preferred if it's easier to fulfill, diminishing the impact that the extant anchors should have. Beyond that, you'd have to check the mechanics of each splat and see if adding in a Vice or Virtue may mess something up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T11:05:41-08:00","id":1468853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EndlessKng</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1467689-vice-ridden-virtuous-merits-on-supernaturals?p=1468846#post1468846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'd have to determine if you can gain willpower from that Virtue/Vice separate from your other anchors, or if fulfilling a Virtue/Vice is mutually exclusive with gaining willpower of that magnitude from another anchor (that is, if you gain via a Vice, you can't regain a single willpower from your Needle or Thread).</div> </div> </div> </div>For the purposes of this thought experiment (or real experiment if anyone wants to actually tries), I'm assuming it simply adds one WP recovering method, <i>ceteris paribus</i>, so we have a willpower recovery method that:<br /> <br /> A) Is optional, being bought as a Merit;<br /> <br /> B) Adds to the flux, increasing rate of recovery;<br /> <br /> C) Thematically follows <b>either</b> human Vice or human Virtue, <b>but not both on the same character</b>; and<br /> <br /> D) Has an uneven distribution in the splat population, as most wouldn't have the Merit, but anyone could have any of the two forms.<br /> <br /> My question would then be, apart from the amp in willpower economy, what would be the implications on the themes of the games? How it can be expect to impact behaviors and mood? How would this impact change based on PC investment (frequency players buy it)? How much would this impact change based on distribution over the splat population, both as it changes frequency in NPCs encountered and as and if it affects how the splat society arranges itself around it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T11:46:27-08:00","id":1468859,"title":"","content":"It's really hard to say. The one big thing that changes is, it does allow for a closer tie between the supernatural and humanity as a whole. That is a potential change in itself. For Promethean, that makes taking such a merit a really big deal - they have human impulses now. I would probably limit the merits to certain levels of Pilgrimage, and suppress them in Centimani (who are not making any progress, and have taken up other urges). Similarly, you'd want to limit it for low-humanity Vampires. <br /> <br /> For werewolves, you also run into the possibility of vices and virtues attracting certain spirits or affecting resonances. Vice-ridden is especially risky for Uratha and Pure, since that can be tied to the Maeljin - incarnations of vice in the Shadow. Virtue isn't significantly better though - Shadow spirits of Virtue are probably more akin to Bayonetta style Angels than benevolent messengers, obsessed with their mission and nature over what's actually good in a given situation. Depending on the circumstances, engaging in either might be a sin against spirit if the action is used to reinforce their humanity, or a sin against the flesh if it causes a spirit to become more powerful to the detriment of the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}